            {
              "name": "國立中興大學學生獎懲委員會組織章程",
              "url": "https://www.osa.nchu.edu.tw/osa/laa/award/award_committee_1091023_3.pdf",
              "text": "國立中興大學學生獎懲委員會組織章程 National Chung Hsing University Student Awards and Discipline Committee Organization Charter 84 年 3 月 11 日本校八十三學年度第二學期臨時校務會議通過 Passed by the university affairs meeting dated on March 11, 1994 92 年 12 月5 日本校九十二學年度第一學期校務會議修正 Amended by the university affairs meeting dated on December 5, 2003 102 年 5 月10 日第 65 次校務會議修正(第 7 條) Amended by the university affairs meeting dated on May 10, 2013 104 年 5 月8 日第 72 次校務會議通過(第 3 條) Passed by the university affairs meeting dated on May 8, 2015 109 年 10 月 23 日第 90 次校務會議通過(第 3 條) Passed by the university affairs meeting dated on October 23, 2020 第一條 為校務推動之順利及學生自治之實踐 ， 依據本校組織規程第十二條 ， 設 立「國立中興大學學生獎懲委員會」 （以下簡稱本會） 。 Article 1: For the smooth promotion of school affairs and the practice of student self- governance, the \"National Chung Hsing University Student Awards and Discipline Committee\" (hereinafter referred to as the Committee) is established in accordance with Article 12 of the University's Organizational Regulations. 第二條 本會依據本校「學生獎懲辦法」 ，審定學生之重大獎懲案。 Article 2: The Committee reviews and approves significant student awards and disciplinary cases in accordance with the University's Student Rewards and Punishment Regulations. 第三條 本會以學生事務長、學生安全輔導室主任、生活輔導組組長、課外活動組 組長、健康及諮商中心主任共五人為當然委員，並由各學院教師各一人及 學生代表四人共同組成之，學生事務長為主任委員。 Article 3: The Committee is composed of the Vice President for Student Affairs, the Director of the Student Safety Division, the Head of Student Life Division, the Head of the Extracurricular Activities Division, and the Director of the Health and Counseling Center, who are all ex-officio members. Additionally, it includes one faculty member from each college and four student representatives. The Dean of Student Affairs serves as the Chairperson of the Committee. 第四條 教師委員由各學院教師互選產生，任期一年，連選得連任一次。 Article 4: Faculty members of the Committee are elected by their peers from each college. The term of office is one year, and they may be re-elected for one consecutive term. 第五條 學生代表由學生會推派之，任期一年。 Article 5: Student representatives are nominated by the Student Union and serve a term of one year. 第六條 本會之委員不得兼任學生申訴評議委員會。 Article 6: Members of the Committee may not concurrently serve on the Student Appeal Review Committee. 第七條 本會每學期開會一次 ， 必要時得召開臨時會議 ， 開會時得邀請有關人員 列席說明。本會會議由主任委員召集，並擔任主席。委員應親自出席會 議，會議須有全體委員二分之一以上出席，始得開議。 Article 7: The Committee meets once each semester, with additional meetings convened as necessary. Relevant personnel may be invited to attend and provide explanations during meetings. The meetings are called and chaired by the Chairperson. Members must attend the meetings in person. A quorum of more than half of the members is required to commence a meeting. 第八條 本章程經校務會議通過後實施，修正時亦同。 Article 8: This charter shall come into effect upon approval by the University Affairs and shall be similarly amended."
            },
            {
              "name": "國立中興大學學生操行成績考評辦法",
              "url": "https://www.osa.nchu.edu.tw/osa/laa/award/award_conduct_1131129_2.pdf",
              "text": "國立中興大學學生操行成績考評辦法 National Chung Hsing University Regulations Governing Student Conduct Evaluation 102 年 3 月 12 日經學生事務會議修正 March 12, 2013 Amended at the Student Affairs Meeting 106 年 4 月 28 日 105 學年度第 2 學期學生事務會議修正 April 28, 2017 amended at the Student Affairs Meeting for the second semester of Academic Year 2016 113 年 11 月 29 日學生事務會議修正(第 3、4、9 條) November 29, 2024 (Articles 3, 4, and 9) amended at the Student Affairs Meeting 第一條 為建立本校學生操行成績考評之依據，特訂定本辦法。 Article 1 The National Chung Hsing University (hereinafter referred to as the University) has formulated the National Chung Hsing University Regulations Governing Student Conduct Evaluation (hereinafter referred to as these Regulations) for the purpose of evaluating student conduct. 第二條 學生操行成績之評定，以八十五分為基本分數，以九十五分為上限， 超過九十五分者，以九十五分計，但得由校長酌予榮譽之獎勵。 Article 2 The base score of student conduct is 85, while the maximum score is 95. Any score above 95 shall be deemed as 95, but the student shall be given an honorary award by the President. 第三條 學生操行分數之等第規定如下： Article 3 The grades corresponding to the conduct scores are as follows: 一、 九十分以上者為優等(相當於 A+)。 I. A+ for a score of 90 or above. 二、 八十分以上不滿九十分為甲等(相當於 A)。 II. A for a score between 80 and 89. 三、 七十分以上不滿八十分為乙等(相當於 B)。 III. B for a score between 70 and 79. 四、 六十分以上不滿七十分為丙等(相當於 C)。 I V. C for a score between 60 and 69. 五、 不滿六十分者為丁等，不及格(相當於 F)。 V. F for a score under 60, which is a failing score. 第四條 學生操行成績每學期視其獎懲表現評定。(由學生事務處依規定核 之)。 Article 4 Students’ conduct grades are assessed each semester based on their reward and penalty performance (to be approved by the Office of Student Affairs in accordance with regulations). 第五條 學生如有獎懲事項，其加減操行成績之規定如下： Article 5 The conduct score shall be added to or deducted from according to rewards and penalties imposed on the students in the following manner: 一、 記嘉獎一次加一分。 I. Add 1 point for 1 commendation; 記小功一次加二﹒五分。 2.5 points for 1 minor merit; 記大功一次加七﹒五分。 7.5 points for 1 major merit. 二、 記申誡一次減一分。 II. Deduct 1 point for 1 reprimand; 記小過一次減二﹒五分。 2.5 points for 1 minor demerit; 記大過一次減七﹒五分。 7.5 points for 1 major demerit. 第六條 導師、相關教師及各單位對學生行為均有建議獎懲之權，請依照本校 學生獎懲辦法之規定程序辦理。 Article 6 Mentors, faculty members and various units in the University have the authority to give recommendations for rewards and penalties, but have to do so in accordance with the University’s Regulations for Student Rewards and Penalties. 第七條 學生操行成績達上限或不及格者，得由學生事務處生活輔導組列舉詳 細事實並說明理由。 Article 7 The Student Life Division of Office of Student Affairs may make a report on students who get a maximum conduct score or a failing score. 第八條 學生操行成績考評後陳請學務長核定之。 Article 8 Students’ conduct grades shall be approved by the Vice President for Student Affairs. 第九條 學生操行成績考評後送教務處與學業成績等一併通知。 Article 9 Students’ conduct grades shall be submitted to the Office of Academic Affairs and notified along with the academic grades. 第十條 本辦法經學生事務會議通過後後陳請校長核定實施，修正時亦同。 Article 10 These Regulations shall be implemented after a resolution is passed by the Student Affairs Meeting and approved by the President. Any amendments hereto shall be processed accordingly."
